  "status": "measured",
  "summary": "fes-f2-gpu on a Modal A100 80GB PCIe, three interleaved runs per arm: whole solver call 0.5009 to 0.2028 ms at 24 unknowns and 0.6310 to 0.2753 ms at 26, from ic before the direct pack (text protocol) to current main (binary protocol); the arms differ by more than one change. Counted answers: 0 of 5 runs differ between the two arms. On main at 24 unknowns the kernel is 0.069 ms, the worker's copies and reply 0.024 ms, the pipe floor (null worker) 0.0135 ms, and about 0.085 ms of the round trip is in none of those phases; the pipe-latency explanation is not supported. The recorded command is the fetch of the finished job by token: the launching client was stopped at its time limit before it could write its own entry (the job itself ran to completion). [pcc:unverified]",
  "validation": null
